{"_v":1,"id":"the-wedding-singer-2006","cat":"broadway","cs":64.38,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":2,"negative":2},"rv":[{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/lifestyle/2006/04/28/the-wedding-singer-broadway-musical-review/","d":"2006-04-28","q":"The Wedding Singer is a cheerful, energetic musical that succeeds in translating the modest charms of the Adam Sandler movie to the Broadway stage."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/729772772/","d":"2006-04-28","q":"Like so much of the show, the designs played with their disco ball and Rubik's Cube patterns make sure we don't miss the obvious."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":66,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2006/legit/reviews/the-wedding-singer-1200512345/","d":"2006-04-27","q":"Like a knockoff Prada bag picked up on Canal Street, this looks at first glance like the real thing, but closer inspection reveals the imperfections."},{"cn":"David Cote","o":"Time Out New York","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/the-wedding-singer","d":"2006-04-27","q":"This agreeable musical adaptation has a sweet, retro flavor that goes down easy, even if it's not particularly nourishing."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"About Entertainment","s":53,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"http://theater.nytimes.com/2006/04/28/theater/reviews/28wedd.html","d":"2006-04-28","q":"True, it consists of little more than winks and nods and quotations."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"http://talkinbroadway.com/world/WeddingSinger.html","d":"2006-04-28","q":"They might have spared Spanger the drenching: She, as with so much else in The Wedding Singer, was, like, already all wet."},{"cn":"Lucy Komisar","o":"The Komisar Scoop","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.thekomisarscoop.com/2007/02/the-wedding-singer-sendups-o